1bb5ef5e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336107/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "577818a1-3045-5404-8f3b-938a82ba7462" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336107/field-4/95beadf825ebf29c5b8f9e1c0c46a4145a155ea067c503ba644e72963fbc7eb5" :answer-field/choices ["q-336107/field-4/18f9c2e6e0c7ccc5ddb88133042a884761c9c24a45964cbfe7bd95b0d691665f" "q-336107/field-4/923adfb52d9d8286b3e761b1629b17c77eb946394f6f63a2dad33874e9e1add7" "q-336107/field-4/dc8611bde8eda73d4c60a5c96c79df36d4a174f7bc8356dca78a972abd23056c" "q-336107/field-4/95beadf825ebf29c5b8f9e1c0c46a4145a155ea067c503ba644e72963fbc7eb5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336107" :question/id #uuid "9fcd6208-dde9-5e8a-b2c1-ff9f0dade0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-336107" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from {{field-1}} by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-3}} by {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ In $\\text{L3}$ we have $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t),$ and in $\\text{L4}$ we have $Φ(t)c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).$ Since both expressions are equal to the same quantity, the transitive property of equality gives $x(t)=Φ(t)c.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3 and L4}$ by the $\\text{the transitive property of equality}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336107/field-1" "q-336107/field-2" "q-336107/field-3" "q-336107/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336107"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336093/field-1/18573b2e60e06250e35d3001e0ffdcac23beadeb3912212e6cd73649cb650489" :answer/id #uuid "647dc60b-9519-5b74-9f4d-9709c601ec9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Φ}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336093/field-1/7f0f2478ce521aa4000523fe155bfe972c7a8cc195da49dd5eb0249ef8194675" :answer/id #uuid "6f63b778-b7dc-5d66-ab9d-9fc9613d6b21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A" 